  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "20261007T090030Z-02f434b3#1",
      "line": 76,
      "path": "tools/ci_checks.py",
      "rule": "R1",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The Darwin bundle prebuild copies the sandbox and fallback policy (`--option sandbox true`, `--option sandbox-fallback false`, the experimental features) as literals inside `run_checks`, and the `justfile` test recipes already state the same policy, so the two can drift apart. Fix: Define the hardened `nix-build` options once as a named constant with a docstring, or add a `just` recipe for the bundle target, and use it in `run_checks` and the test."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261007T090030Z-02f434b3#2",
      "line": 365,
      "path": "reports/20261007-darwin-bundle-scheduling/validate.py",
      "rule": "R10",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "Each check in the validator is a bare `assert` with no message, so a failure shows only `AssertionError` and a line number: it does not say which payload or field failed, or what the user can do next. Fix: Raise errors with messages that name the file or field that failed and say how to find the cause, for example \"compare raw-sha256.json with the retained gzip files\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261007T090030Z-02f434b3#3",
      "line": 367,
      "path": "reports/20261007-darwin-bundle-scheduling/validate.py",
      "rule": "R1",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The expected counts 16, 12 and 42 are literals inside `validate`, and only the docstring of `RAW_MANIFEST_SHA256` explains one of them. Fix: Define named constants with docstrings, for example `RETAINED_PAYLOAD_COUNT`, `ORIGINAL_PAYLOAD_COUNT` and `BUNDLE_CASE_COUNT`, and use them in `validate`."
    }
  ],
